# Anchored with a leading slash, deliberately. An unanchored `release/` matches at ANY depth and
# silently swallowed docs/release/README.txt -- the readme that ships inside the download.
/build/
/build-tests/
/dist/
/release/
/out/
.vs/
*.user

# `extern/` is NOT ignored. It was, and that was the bug: `extern/CommonLibSSE-NG` is a submodule
# the build needs and `extern/SKSEMenuFramework.h` is a vendored header it compiles, so ignoring
# the directory shipped a repository that could not configure.
